To create an IAM policy that grants read-only access to a single S3 bucket, you can use the following policy structure:

```
{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": [
            "s3:GetObject",
            "s3:ListBucket"
        ],
        "Resource": [
            "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name",
            "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*"
        ]
    }
}
```

Just replace `your-bucket-name` with the actual name of the S3 bucket for which you want to grant read-only access. This policy will allow the user to list the contents of the bucket and retrieve objects from it.

